# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/draft-vocab four-card DEVELOPMENT window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/draft-vocab and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dvocab-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-dvocab-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# D-V1: the SAME-IMAGE CONTROL tau arm of D-V2. It MUST run before D-V2 on this image: D-V2's C2_TAULAB_PAIR_CONTROL is the run id of THIS job, and the pair report refuses runs whose image tags
# differ. NOTE the run id of this job's workflow run. The CONTROL tau arm: the default drafter (dedf8df6) on image tp4-dvocab-1. A3 (the calibration: the lanes' 4 x 4k and 4 x 32k prompts, thinking OFF)
# runs on THIS arm only and must reproduce the served drafter's own reference within +/-7%; then A1 and A2. Thinking ON, coding-agent turns from the public SWE-rebench set (A1) and the scrubbed own-session
# set (A2) as the lab already uses, no customer traffic; the data directory is rig-local and read-only to the job, checked against its manifest before the container starts. The serving profile is
# c2-packed-tp4 with the lab's two arithmetic-neutral log flags and, for a drafter arm, only that arm's drafter-only flag. Duration (estimate): 90 min (the deadline of 85 min is counted from the container
# start, the load included). Kill rule: A3 runs FIRST on this arm and a FAIL stops it before A1 and A2, which voids the window's tau arms; a launched-argv problem line refuses the arm and exits 2; the canary
# or the breaker stopping the lab, or a stall, ends the arm.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset taulab
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dvocab-1
C2_TAULAB_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_TAULAB_DRAFTER_ARM=control
C2_TAULAB_ARMS=A3 A1 A2
C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE=85
C2_TAULAB_IN_FLIGHT=8
